+From 4648be34631b4aabf52e88db28cbc882065923d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: local <l@l>
+Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:13:56 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] Headless GPU image renderers: Ganesh (EGL/GL, Vulkan) and
+ Graphite (Vulkan)
+
+Offscreen renderers that paint the same SkiaScenePainter commands into a GPU
+render target and read the pixels back, for servers without a window or
+display: SkiaGpuImageRenderer (Ganesh; OpenGL through an EGL device and a
+surfaceless context, or Vulkan without surface extensions) and
+SkiaGraphiteImageRenderer (Graphite on Vulkan). Both report per-frame
+record/submit/wait/readback times and may share one device per thread.
+
+skia-safe's "gl" becomes the default feature "ganesh-gl" (the window
+renderer needs it), so that a Graphite-only Skia binary can be used:
+rust-skia publishes no binary with both Ganesh and Graphite. Graphite drops
+draws of raster images, and rust-skia does not bind Recorder image
+providers, so the scene painter uploads images with the recorder first.
+
+Also: purge_font_cache() for retention measurements.
