+From 2daa4f8b9332401fd7f09e4840e334f0fbb1a041 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: local <l@l>
+Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:17:29 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Headless GPU renderers: render into a caller's buffer;
+ pipelined readback
+
+render_timed() takes the output slice from the caller (Option<&mut [u8]>,
+exactly width x height x 4 bytes) instead of resizing a Vec, so a frame
+can be read back straight into memory the embedder owns (a Node Buffer,
+a shared ring) with no extra copy. The length is checked.
+
+Experimental pipelined readback for SkiaGpuImageRenderer, so the CPU can
+record frame N+1 while the GPU draws frame N:
+- PipelineMode::Deferred (GL or Vulkan): a ring of up to 8 surfaces;
+  pipeline_submit() records and submits without waiting,
+  pipeline_complete() reads the oldest frame back (synchronously).
+- PipelineMode::GlPbo (GL): right after submit, glReadPixels into a
+  pixel-pack buffer plus a fence; pipeline_complete() waits on the fence
+  and maps the buffer. Skia's GL state is reset after the raw GL calls.
+  rust-skia does not bind Ganesh's asyncRescaleAndReadPixels, so this is
+  done with the gl crate on the renderer's own context.
+Frames complete in submit order; a full pipeline rejects submits;
+pipeline_stop() waits for the GPU and discards frames in flight, and an
+abandoned context is reported instead of read.
